{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "The plan-review round budget is charged per plan LINEAGE (declared predecessor, -vN name shape, shared work item -- the item-108 resolver) with a hard cap of FIVE successful reviewer invocations, period. A successor plan, split, rename, copy, or new branch inherits every round its lineage already spent and never refills the budget. run-plan-review refuses a launch past the lineage cap; the former succession-chain advisory numbers are unchanged but the budget itself now enforces. Measured motivation: ~30 recorded rounds across stacked successor branches, each round legal under the retired per-file count.",
    "The capped finalize (release valve) opens on the LINEAGE's spend and accepts any lineage member's loadable manifest as its classified-predecessor proof, so a spent lineage always has a working exit that points at the build -- refusal binds launching more review, never the exit (the 2026-07-14 deadlock rule, kept at lineage level).",
    "A capped finalize now records every carried finding into the plan document's committed Cross-Model Review Evidence block -- severity, focus id, summary, and a FINAL PLAN banner -- so the plan itself is the final plan and carries its own unresolved findings into implementation. The block rides the hash-excluded evidence section, so recording findings can never void the evidence that produced them.",
    "The run meta records the lineage-derived effective round, so finalize's convergence checks and carried stamps see the lineage position; the hard-cap refusal, successor instruction, and chain advisory no longer prescribe decomposition or successor plans as a budget remedy; the printed exits are finalize-capped-and-build or carry-findings-and-build. The convergence ladder widens to rounds 3-5 self-authorized with a recorded --exception-note; the two-round convergence target is unchanged."
  ],
